      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d provide more details here (so that we don\u0027t forget):\n\n1. Without disabling CONFIG_INTEL_IOMMU_PERF_EVENTS fatcat doesn\u0027t boot if CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL is enabled. The reason is unknown. We can enable it back once we find and fix the root cause.\n2. Without enabling CONFIG_IRQ_REMAP and CONFIG_INTEL_IOMMU_SVM fatcat doesn\u0027t boot, regardless of CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL. The reason is unknown.\n3. Enabling CONFIG_IRQ_REMAP is useful anyway, not just on fatcat but on any x86 platform, since x2APIC depends on it. So we should keep CONFIG_IRQ_REMAP enabled even after fixing the root cause of fatcat boot issues.",
      "revId": "b4fc0c6407433ca4ccc4d2898e18f618f912add9",
